# Go module workflow (this repo)

**Scope:** Root module `github.com/behaviorengineering/gitboard`. Workspace: root `go.work` includes `.` only. strop is a normal module require (see `architecture.mdc`).

## Forbidden

- MUST NOT run `go mod init` or delete root `go.mod` / `go.sum` or `go.work`.
- MUST NOT recreate module layout or duplicate Makefile targets that already exist.
- MUST NOT change import paths to "fix" tests without a stated reason.
- MUST NOT re-add a `providers/strop` submodule or commit a long-lived `replace` for strop unless the user explicitly asks.
- MUST NOT implement gitboard features by permanently forking strop inside this repo; change strop upstream, tag, then `go get`.

## Required

- MUST use existing `go.mod`, `go.sum`, `go.work`, and Makefile targets (`make build`, `make test`, `make vet`, `make ci`).
- MUST run `go mod tidy` after adding or removing dependencies, then `go mod verify` when checking integrity.
- For temporary local strop work: sibling checkout + `go.work` `use` path (see `architecture.mdc`); drop it before merge once the published tag is bumped.

## Commands

- Correct: `go mod tidy`, `make test`, `make build`, `go build ./...`, `make ci`.
- Wrong: `go mod init new_module`, `rm go.mod go.sum`.

## On failure

- MUST fix test logic or application code, not the module skeleton.
- MUST add missing dependencies via `go.mod` and `go mod tidy`, not workarounds.
